    "narrative": "The core of our lineup today is anchored by **Corbin Carroll** (87.14), who draws an elite matchup against Miles Mikolas. His score is bolstered by a rare confluence of a favorable park and a slow opposing delivery that screams stolen base potential\u2014the primary currency of our roster. Complementing him are **Isaac Paredes** (72.13), **Austin Riley** (71.27), and **Gabriel Moreno** (70.58). **Isaac Paredes** benefits significantly from a 19% boost against the projected SP_xERA of Erick Fedde, while **Austin Riley** leverages a massive 16% park factor uplift, making them high-ceiling plays despite the lineup uncertainty. **James Wood** (69.70) remains a set-and-forget option given his elite 0.423 xwOBA, proving that even against a tough lefty, his underlying metrics are too potent to bench.\n\nOur most difficult decision of the morning was keeping **Seiya Suzuki** (47.00) on the bench. While his score represents a solid, reliable floor, he failed to crack our top-tier starting slots, primarily because the optimizer prioritized the specific situational advantages\u2014such as favorable platoon splits or SP delivery speeds\u2014offered by players like **Mickey Moniak** or **Henry Bolte**. **Seiya Suzuki** was edged out by the superior projected efficiency of our lower-order starters who possess better matchup-adjusted profiles. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given that nearly our entire lineup relies on pending official confirmations. **Josh Naylor** (49.91) is a primary concern; facing the legendary Jacob deGrom presents a significant challenge, resulting in a 19% penalty to his base projection. Similarly, **Jose Caballero** (48.26) and **Mickey Moniak** (49.57) are navigating difficult pitching matchups. We have successfully avoided the below-floor trap, ensuring that everyone currently slated to play maintains at least a 45+ score. We will monitor the pre-game lineups closely to ensure that our assumed batting orders for **Dalton Rushing**, **Brice Turang**, and others do not shift downward, which would necessitate immediate adjustments to our game cap strategy.",
